WEBVTT

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:04.210
Another year's gone by,
and she still hasn't learned her lesson.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.590
Otherwise known
as "The Day I Feel Sorry for Higashida."

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:14.300
Kamakura, do something so Higashida
isn't transformed by that chocolate.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.470
Use the power of money.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.220
Instead of that,

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.390
it'd be faster to fiddle with Higashida
and turn him into a cyborg.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:23.690
Transform Higashida
so he can't be transformed...

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.810
So no matter what,
he'll be transformed, huh?

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:27.320
FEBRUARY

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.020
Poor guy.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:03.910
FATE SURVIVAL

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.330
Yuuta!

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.420
Here.

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.500
Is this money?

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.460
Have you finally
turned over a new leaf, she-devil?

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:14.630
You're shaken up, huh?

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:18.640
Come on, Yuuta.
Have you forgotten what a reward is?

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:21.140
This is...

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.270
That's right, lottery tickets.
And they're all losers!

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.100
I don't want 'em!

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.190
But you never know.

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:30.650
I ordered Tasaka and the others
to get all losing tickets,

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.940
but maybe they made a mistake
and there's a winner mixed in here.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:39.200
There's even a possibility
that one of these tickets is worth a fortune.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.370
PICKED NUMBERS

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.910
Well, it's up to you
whether you check them or not, Yuuta.

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.960
Ignorant people are entrusted with dreams
just based on scraps of paper.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.370
Pathetic, isn't it?

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:51.460
Even though you know they're all losers,

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:54.670
you cling to a tiny hope
and check them all anyway.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.880
It's incredibly unsightly.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:00.470
I'm so kind to give you that hope!

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:02.640
Clean that crap up.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:05.600
M-Make a fool out of me? Dammit!

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.100
You're actually checking them.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:08.180
Here you are.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:11.650
Sorry. You buy for me every time...

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:15.230
Oh, this time I changed the plan
and made my own.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:18.900
What's wrong, Adachi?

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.490
Don't ask me.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.240
Mura, did you do something?

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:23.740
I didn't do a thing.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:25.790
After all, he's unconscious!

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:27.200
All I did...

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.370
It had to be something scary!

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.750
I've failed every time
trying to make chocolate!

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:36.550
But this time is different!

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:39.420
The reason is I had an assistant this time!

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.970
Shut up. Just give it to me.

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:45.760
Well, well, Nagata...

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.970
Did you make the chocolate
this time, Nagata?

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:48.850
Higashida!

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:51.140
No. I helped.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:53.900
You helped, Nagata?

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.520
It must've been tough.

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:57.900
Yes. Um, it was...

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:04.910
<i>If you melt the store-bought
ingredients first, you shouldn't really fail.</i>

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:05.580
<i>Right!</i>

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.910
<i>As long as you don't add anything
that's inedible. Just kidding!</i>

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:10.790
<i>You don't add any?</i>

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:14.040
There were various surprises. Um...

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.670
She put you to a lot of trouble.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:17.250
Miss...

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.380
Higashida is even scarier.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:22.840
I-It's okay! I'm sure he's nervous, too!

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:24.640
You did your best to make that, right?

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:25.850
Good lu—

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:30.140
<i>Huh? It's strange for me
to wish her good luck, isn't it?</i>

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:34.270
<i>When I think about it, I like Higashida,
so it's weird for me to cheer on Miyakoshi.</i>

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.770
<i>But if she doesn't do her best,
Higashida will be in trouble!</i>

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:40.650
<i>The feeling of wanting to support
Miyakoshi is, um, is, um...</i>

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.110
Good luck!

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:43.070
<i>To me!</i>

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:47.530
H-Here!

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.280
Thanks.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:56.750
N-Nothing's happening!

00:04:58.750 --> 00:04:59.750
Did I fail?

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:00.920
You succeeded!

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:01.880
Nagata...

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:02.970
Y-Yes?

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:07.720
I'm very sorry for always
giving you so much trouble.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:08.720
Higa—

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.390
It's definitely not your fault,
Nagata, so don't worry.

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:14.560
That was my one concern.

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.560
And with that said, goodbye...

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.520
Higashida!

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:23.110
Even though his face is bluish-purple,
he's got a dazzling smile!

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.170
<i>Shake it up, baby!</i>

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:40.750
<i>Are you up, Higashida?</i>

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:45.930
<i>Why are you going
back to sleep, Higashida?</i>

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:47.840
<i>I came up with it.</i>

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:50.390
<i>The reason you come here.</i>

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.180
<i>Even though it's not in your jurisdiction,</i>

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:55.140
<i>I appreciate you going to all the trouble.</i>

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:57.650
<i>Cooking is made up of the love
between the person who eats</i>

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:00.150
<i>and the person who prepares the food.</i>

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:04.400
<i>I realized you two don't have that.</i>

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:09.620
<i>Therefore, Higashida, you should
love Miyakoshi with all your heart.</i>

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.460
What was bad about it?

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.210
<i>That's what I want to ask.</i>

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:18.920
Higashida, I'm sorry.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:21.210
Even though we don't like
each other at all,

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.840
I almost kill you every time
with my chocolate.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:25.970
Miyakoshi, cheer up.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:30.550
Higashida once told me
to give chocolate to the person I like,

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:32.060
but I don't like anyone.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:33.430
The person I like?

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:35.680
If I come to like him, I can do anything?

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:36.640
No!

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:39.850
<i>I thought you were furious,
but now you're crying!</i>

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:44.440
<i>I recommended you proceed
with make-believe love.</i>

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:47.740
<i>That would only result
in Miyakoshi getting hurt, too.</i>

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:48.950
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:51.620
<i>No. It's not about getting hurt.</i>

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:56.710
<i>The thing is,
Miyakoshi just isn't my type.</i>

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:02.750
<i>Pretend you didn't hear
my suggestion and go home.</i>

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:06.720
Higashida!

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:08.930
Thank goodness, right, Miyakoshi?

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:12.680
Yes! Higashida,
I'm sorry again for everything!

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:15.430
Somehow, I'll definitely get better
at cooking for next time

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.520
and make something edible,
so forgive me!

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:19.020
<i>Get good at cooking...</i>

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:22.690
<i>In other words, I would have to
love Miyakoshi with all my heart.</i>

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:24.730
Don't worry about it.

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:27.610
That's okay.
You don't have to console me.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:28.820
No, really.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:32.410
You can continue to be lousy
at cooking. I'll keep eating it.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:37.120
You can stop worrying about whether
it's good or bad or a matter of life and death.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:42.330
In fact, I like you this way,
unable to cook, Miyakoshi.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:44.540
H-Higashida...

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.920
When you're nice to me, I feel...

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:48.590
totally grossed-out!

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:49.550
That's the spirit!

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:53.510
<i>Will these two always have
a relationship like this, with love mixed in?</i>

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:59.100
Hana-hana and Naga are busy
with Valentine's Day stuff,

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.190
and it feels like I've been left behind.

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:03.480
So I bought some chocolate on a whim.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:07.320
I feel sorry for you, Kouno,
so I was going to give it to you...

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:09.490
Drip...

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:12.530
but it looks really good,
so would you mind if I ate it myself?

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:14.160
Eat it.

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:21.790
So I wonder what happened
with Shindou's lottery tickets.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.250
I won!

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:25.130
I checked them all,
and one's worth 300 yen!

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:29.630
Huh? What are those looks
of pity for? I'm happy!

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:32.220
Saiki helped me!

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:34.050
I yelped.

00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:35.890
I HELPED.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:35.890
You know...

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:37.930
the time it took
to check all those tickets,

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:39.850
you would've made
more money by just working.

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.060
This is why you're poor.

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:47.020
Wh-What the hell?

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:50.490
I-I didn't put a winning ticket
in there because I like you.

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:53.660
I figured if I put
even a cheap winner in the bunch,

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:55.120
you'd waste effort looking for it.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:55.990
Shiho!

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:03.250
Thanks to you, I won 300 yen,
so put it towards this month's payment.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.460
Thank you so much!

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:08.130
What's with you? That ticks me off!

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:09.840
Wh-Why?

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:11.090
Adachi...

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:15.640
The person who just ordered
doesn't like scallions, so leave them out.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:16.970
Sure.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:18.680
I'm counting on you.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:22.560
Um... Why are you talking
with your back turned towards me?

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:25.100
I wouldn't want you to faint again.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:26.440
I know, right?

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.030
Faint?

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:34.490
Of course that would
make Muranushi mad.

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:35.820
I know, right?

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:38.700
This is work, so I'm sure
she's just trying to be nice,

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:42.000
but it's homemade,
so she did put some feelings into it.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.620
Therefore, you have
an obligation to accept it.

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:46.460
<i>It doesn't matter
who it's from or what it is.</i>

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:47.290
Right?

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.590
<i>Those are the eyes of a man
who's been through a war.</i>

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:54.170
On the other hand, it seems
you don't really like Muranushi,

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.510
so don't bother forcing yourself.

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:56.260
Huh?

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:57.430
"Huh?"

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:59.930
After all, when she talks to you,
you turn pale,

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:01.890
avoid making eye contact
and act all scared.

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:05.020
It's obvious to me that you dislike her.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:06.730
Adachi?

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:10.110
Um... Uh...
You know horror movies...

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:16.570
Yeah. There are people who are scared of
horror movies, but they watch them anyway.

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:19.570
- It's the same kind of thing.
- Sorry for being a horror movie.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.280
You were standing there!

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:25.080
I was. I'm working, so of course
that's where I'm going to be.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:26.920
Do you have a problem with that?

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:27.870
No.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:32.840
Adachi, I don't like it when someone
is whispering about me behind my back,

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:35.920
so if there's something you want to say,
would you say it to my face?

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:38.220
But, um... Uh...

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:40.720
How can I explain it, uh, Muranushi...

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:43.060
What? Spit it out.

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:45.770
- S-Sorry...
- A-Are they fighting?

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:45.770
SORRY

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:48.810
Muranushi, try not to be mad at him.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:50.730
I'm not mad. It's just...

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:54.480
He fainted in response
to my homemade chocolate

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:56.610
and then compared me
to a horror movie.

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:58.820
I'm just saying, "What's up with that?"

00:10:58.820 --> 00:10:59.990
You're mad, aren't you?

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:05.120
This horror movie's homemade chocolate
is as lethal as Miyakoshi's chocolate, huh?

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:07.120
No, Muranushi, that's too extreme!

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:09.620
- Don't compare it to that stuff!
- What?

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:13.840
Muranushi, I feel really bad
about all of that.

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.630
I've been totally rude.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:18.880
Being scared
just because you talked to me...

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:23.010
Even though you did nothing to harm me,
and your cooking isn't like Miyakoshi.

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:27.230
On top of that, I fainted
after you gave me homemade chocolate.

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:30.190
Your cooking isn't Miyakoshi's
cooking! I'm sorry!

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:32.610
Okay, okay. Calm down.

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:35.860
The chocolate was delicious.

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:40.860
Anyway, I won't be scared
or run away or turn pale anymore.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:41.990
Really?

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.030
Yeah!

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:44.910
Really?

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:49.910
- Yeah!
- You withstood it.

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:53.920
I understand, so we can forget
about what happened this time.

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:54.790
Thank you.

00:11:55.050 --> 00:11:57.920
By the way, why did you
make homemade chocolate this time?

00:11:58.130 --> 00:11:59.130
The reason is...

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:00.300
Adachi...

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:01.800
I figured...

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:05.810
you'd be extremely surprised by it.

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:10.350
So it turned out just as you wanted.
I was so surprised that I fainted.

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:11.900
But you got angry.

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:12.850
That's true.

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:15.770
You all piss me off!

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:21.400
What's the harm?
Those two patched things up.

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:23.700
And I was moved.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:28.370
It was the moment your cooking
became useful for the first time ever.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:31.710
I was right. There's no sense
bending over backwards trying to improve.

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:33.420
Stay just as you are.

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:36.710
<i>Higashida has been nice
to me like this lately.</i>

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:38.630
Jeez.

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:40.590
It really is scary.

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:44.930
What if my cooking's become a habit
for him and now he can't get enough?

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.260
I don't think that's it.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:47.470
Impossible.

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:53.060
<i>Miyakoshi must actually hate Higashida</i>

00:12:53.310 --> 00:12:55.860
<i>if she dislikes it when he smiles
at her or speaks kindly.</i>

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:57.440
<i>But she's lucky...</i>

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:00.900
<i>If Higashida smiled at me...</i>

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:03.660
<i>...maybe I'd be a little scared.</i>

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:06.160
Naga... It's written all over your face.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:09.540
I'm done with all this
chocolate sweet stuff.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:12.460
I've decided to give up on chocolate!

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:15.250
<i>Even though she said she'd feed him
chocolate until he died...</i>

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:18.170
My late grandpa said something
a long time ago...

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:21.550
I'm gonna feed Higashida
a variety of things!

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:25.260
"Nothing good comes of a woman's resolve."

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:28.260
That's what Miyakoshi said?

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:30.520
I wonder what's wrong.

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:33.270
I wish she would've stayed
the way she was.

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:35.190
<i>- What's wrong?
- What's wrong?</i>

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:40.820
Is Higashida okay?

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:42.690
In more ways than one, huh?

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:45.950
It doesn't look like he's going to
get together with Hana-hana,

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:51.080
so do your best to make your love for Higashi
bear fruit and still hang out with me.

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:52.750
Yanagiba...

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.040
My love...

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:55.710
What do I do...

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:58.040
<i>...if it does bear fruit?</i>

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:00.500
Naga...

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:10.350
When you have as much money
as milady Shiho,

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:13.640
there's a high likelihood
that something dangerous will happen.

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:15.230
Listen, newbie!

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:17.150
It's our job to protect at a time like that

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:20.230
and most of all, prevent any crime
from being committed.

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:22.320
Tasaka, it seems...

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:24.940
she can handle herself fine.

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:27.070
Idiot! It's the man we're protecting!

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:28.620
The man...

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:31.950
<i>Until just recently,</i>

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:35.370
<i>she was merciless
but smiled normally and seemed happy.</i>

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:37.250
<i>After buying that
Japanese sword, though,</i>

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:40.840
<i>she's been oddly kind to Shindou and
sometimes has a faraway look in her eyes.</i>

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:44.670
<i>Those eyes tell me
she intends to kill Shindou!</i>

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:48.180
Did that blond guy do something to her?

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:51.970
He did and he didn't.
Well, it was a long time ago.

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:53.140
A-A long time ago...

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:54.600
It happens, right?

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:58.350
Because of your youth, you do or say
something that can't be undone.

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:00.270
It does happen.

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:01.610
It does.

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:04.820
Maybe we should
get those guys some tea.

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:07.240
I'm on break now, so I'll get it.

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:11.240
Anyway, those bangs look
like they'd be too hot for comfort.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:12.700
Isn't it hard for you to see through that?

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:15.950
No. Unless it's this length,
I can't make eye contact with people.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:18.080
Um... Have some tea.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:20.040
Thank you.

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:27.260
Y-You're Sayuri Muranushi, aren't you?

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:29.470
Yes, that's right.

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:31.760
We met ten years ago!

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:33.640
Don't tell me you've forgotten!

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:40.900
Long time no see... Yamagishi?

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:44.360
Dammit! No!
You friggin' forgot about me!

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:47.400
It's Saitou! Saitou! Daichi Saitou!

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:47.400
DAICHI SAITOU

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:53.530
We were in the same class
in elementary school... Dammit!

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:55.660
I remember a Saitou.

00:15:56.750 --> 00:15:59.080
You're the Saitou who was about to cry

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:02.460
when you lifted a girl's skirt
on the way home from school, right?

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:03.840
You don't remember me!

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:05.630
Acquaintance of yours?

00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:06.800
Yes, I suppose.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:12.300
He was a classmate in elementary school
who'd tease me about everything.

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:13.680
<i>Hey, Muranushi!</i>

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:16.970
<i>That ghost-like face of yours
has never smiled, I'll bet!</i>

00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:26.900
I thought I'd smile at him
to teach him a lesson,

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:30.280
but after that,
Saitou totally had the blues.

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:34.780
At the time, I didn't really
understand my own power.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:39.250
<i>You talk like your smile
is a weapon, but is it really?</i>

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:42.870
At any rate, you've changed.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:44.130
It's your fault!

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:47.840
Ever since that incident, I haven't been
able to look anyone in the eye.

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:50.260
Socially, it's been an extreme hardship.

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:53.720
It's your fault
I had to take this crappy jo—

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:57.850
I'm sorry, Muranushi.
Sorry about my "thing" here.

00:16:57.470 --> 00:16:59.850
THING

00:16:58.560 --> 00:16:59.390
Not at all.

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:00.890
Wh-What do you think you're doing?

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:02.770
"What do you think you're doing?"
is my line!

00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:07.440
When I'm here, the other employees
are basically the same rank as me.

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:12.570
You've got a defiant attitude
against one of those people.

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:16.620
Know your place, you low-level jerk.

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:18.950
You know what I mean by "low-level"?

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:19.910
There you are.

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:23.120
I'll let you off the hook this time,

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:26.080
but from now on, I expect you
to be much more obedient.

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:27.460
Um...

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:31.630
It seems that it's my fault
you've had various obstacles in your life.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:35.470
And apologizing won't change
anything, but I'm sorry.

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:38.140
You don't owe him an apology!

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:42.350
As a fellow sadist,
that's not like you, Muranushi!

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:44.190
I'm not a sadist.

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:48.480
His hair has turned white, too.
I feel responsible.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:49.320
I...

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:53.070
I just dye my hair!

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:55.240
Don't worry about that, idiot!

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:58.490
He just abandoned his post.
That takes some nerve.

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:00.660
It's always been like that with me.

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:04.750
In front of me,
the boy is stressed out or angry,

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:08.130
but just when I think he hates me,
it seems that's not the case.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:09.880
That's...

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:13.090
I wonder why. It's strange.

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:14.340
Very strange.

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:17.470
<i>I have to come up
with a snappy comeback here?</i>

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:27.440
I'm definitely fired, dammit.

00:18:27.690 --> 00:18:30.650
Nothing good can come
of getting mixed up with Muranushi.

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:35.700
I've been looking for you.

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:39.280
You blame Muranushi
for your life turning out lousy.

00:18:39.530 --> 00:18:41.660
Miserable, low-level Saitou.

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:44.910
It's pathetic how you let the past
linger your whole life long.

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:49.380
Milady Shiho is incredibly blind
to her own shortcomings.

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:53.250
The funny thing is you actually had
a crush on Muranushi, right?

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:54.210
No!

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:57.510
There are warped people who are in love
with someone but pretend not to be.

00:18:57.510 --> 00:19:01.550
They are mean to that person
just to get their attention.

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:05.560
I wonder why those people waste
so much time and effort on that,

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:09.980
when the person they like
just ends up thinking they're hated.

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:13.940
Shut your face! I can do what I want!

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:18.200
I know you're gonna fire me anyway,
so leave me alone.

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:22.120
I can't work in an environment
if Muranushi is there. But it can't be helped.

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:23.910
I'm not going to fire you.

00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:26.500
But I'm totally useless!

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:27.750
You're fine.

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.750
<i>Milady is kind to kindred spirits.</i>

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:35.960
Maybe you'll put me to work
somewhere Muranushi isn't?

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:40.510
I'll do everything I can to see to it
that you're always around Muranushi!

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:45.970
You should suffer with the complicated
feeling that may be joy or misery!

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:49.060
<i>Milady, you hate kindred spirits?</i>

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:54.610
Hello.

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:55.780
Hello.

00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:57.940
I'm here to work!

00:19:58.650 --> 00:19:59.860
I know.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:04.530
Yanagiba...

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:07.000
Why don't you go to school already?

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:09.120
Higashi, you're always
on my case about that.

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:12.750
The next time you eat
Hana-hana's chocolate, become nicer.

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:14.630
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:19.760
We just had Valentine's Day, so I'm not
going to eat chocolate for a long time.

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:21.220
Right, Miyakoshi?

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:23.090
I'm coming up with a plan!

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:25.140
Even if you say that
with a service smile, forget it!

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:27.390
You think I'm just gonna let you
feed me on a regular basis?

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:29.390
The poison from last time
hasn't left my system yet!

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:30.980
What the heck? Miser!

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:33.940
If you think about it,
I only made it for you three times!

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:36.650
At this rate, who knows
when I'll hit upon a success?

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:37.570
Since we've come this far,

00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:40.490
I'm gonna keep making stuff
until you declare it's delicious!

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:42.700
Let me get some more experience here!

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:45.950
I've had it up to here
with near-death experiences!

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:48.450
B-Besides...

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:52.120
<i>Higashida, you should love
Miyakoshi with all your heart.</i>

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:54.000
<i>All your heart... All your heart...</i>

00:20:54.290 --> 00:20:55.960
<i>That's the one thing I won't do!</i>

00:20:56.420 --> 00:20:57.710
Instead...

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:00.630
I like the Miyakoshi who can't cook!

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:04.140
I don't need you to like me.

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:07.100
REJECTED

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:11.020
That's right.

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:14.230
When you think about it,
it's crazy, isn't it?

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:17.360
The two of us arguing,
you making chocolate, giving it to me...

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:18.730
All over a little chocolate...

00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:20.940
SO FURIOUS
THAT SHE'S TONGUE-TIED FOR A MOMENT

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.240
Valentine's Day is ridiculous, too.

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:26.120
I'll never eat your cooking, Miyakoshi,
not for the rest of my life!

00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:28.120
In the first place, I'm not obliged to!

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:29.490
Higashida, that was cruel!

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:32.710
<i>I was listening, and Miyakoshi
is definitely the one who's cruel!</i>

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:35.630
Well, my shift is over, so I'm going home.

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:40.260
I no longer have to live in fear
of your cooking. Life is good.

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:41.720
Oh, that's right.

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:44.590
I don't want you
to like me either, Miyakoshi,

00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:46.340
so we're on the same page, huh?

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:50.310
Good work.

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:54.230
Wh-Why was he so angry?

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:56.060
Miyakoshi...

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:36.080
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:29.700
So Higashida's raccoon is plumping up!

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:31.490
He must be feeding it something good!

00:23:31.490 --> 00:23:32.620
<i>Well, that's because
Mom makes me delicious food!</i>

00:23:31.990 --> 00:23:32.910
Nice and plump.

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:34.080
<i>You want to kill me?!</i>

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:35.200
Next time, "Cooking is Love."

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:36.080
COOKING IS LOVE
